{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/67327-of-shadows-yet-to-come-and-vague-rules-spoilers-ahead","id":67327,"title":"Of Shadows Yet To Come and Vague Rules. (Spoilers Ahead)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-07T12:19:27-08:00","id":67327,"title":"Of Shadows Yet To Come and Vague Rules. (Spoilers Ahead)","content":"~~I'm glad to hear they're working to revamp the rules and mechanics of Scion... I've recently started a game; and I'm starting with Of Shadows Yet To Come. Granted, my players have made their own characters instead of pre-gen, but storyline-wise it's easy to work with.<br /> Things were going fine until they ran into the oni. I didn't manage to hit any of them (though I did total one of the Bands vehicles), but that was largely due to poor rolls. However, they were doing well in hitting (not hard when one of the Band has Giantbane), but it was fairly impossible to bypass the oni's ridiculous Soak. He has Epic Stamina, just like some of the Scions.. but unless I missed something, you get to subtract your Soak from EVERY HIT. This is going to come to a point of a slobberknocker, which would be epic, -if- it didn't wind up dragging down into a pointless swing-fest because no one can get actual damage in. ...Am I missing something here?<br /> Point the second. Aggravated damage. Can we be any more vague? It's stated a few times, as damage that affects &quot;the soul.&quot; Okay. Tells me nothing. In the vast history of WW games, fire has always done Agg damage. One of my players had a brilliant idea to set the oni on fire; cool; it worked.. but absolutely NO rules on fire as a source of damage, on how much it would feasibly do, if it counts as Agg or not...<br /> My players and I all love the 'fluff'. But if we can expect this sort of 'crunch', I'm not sure I'll continue using the current Scion system. Does anyone have any insight into this issue so I don't pull my hair out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2221-dtorakhan","name":"DTorakhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T12:46:44-08:00","id":67344,"title":"","content":"1) It is normal, an Oni is a very powerful opponent against Heroes. I suggest you to take a look at the characters stats and see what is the average roll to hit and to damage and calculate the enemies DV and Soak with the intent of making combat last a given amount of actions.<br /> <br /> 2) Aggravated damage is very rare for the maximum Aggravated soak someone has is 10 (from Epic Stamina) plus their armor's Aggravated soak (equal to its Lethal soak). The only sources of Aggravated damage is either indicated in the powers the characters use or is defined as some weakness.<br /> <br /> 2.1) I believe Fire is Aggravated damage in WW history, because it is one of the Vampires' weaknesses, but I don't believe it even extends beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T14:26:15-08:00","id":67414,"title":"","content":"I recall a humorous point one of my gaming group found once in the OWoD involving fire dealing agg. damage. Namely that they didn't put in any caveat, so even fire elementals took agg damage from fire. :B I understand oni are supposed to be tough as hell. My big thing was, looking at all the dice and stats, only one of my PCs could have managed to deal damage to it, and that would involve the HIGHLY unlikely event of him rolling successes on every damage die. The oni fight is supposed to be tough, but not unwinnable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2221-dtorakhan","name":"DTorakhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T02:51:10-08:00","id":67810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DTorakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/67327-of-shadows-yet-to-come-and-vague-rules-spoilers-ahead?p=67414#post67414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand oni are supposed to be tough as hell. My big thing was, looking at all the dice and stats, only one of my PCs could have managed to deal damage to it, and that would involve the HIGHLY unlikely event of him rolling successes on every damage die. The oni fight is supposed to be tough, but not unwinnable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was where you failed, after a couple of hit and misses you should have fudged the results. For example, if you had decreased the soak of the oni by 1 each time they failed to deal damage until they hit the problem would have been solved.<br /> <br /> Other suggestion would be to see that it was a standoff and so the Oni leaves the players with whatever they want due to his master's orders, he was tired, he got what he was looking for... That way the plot could continue to move and the players would see that they cannot defeat all enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T18:04:25-08:00","id":68735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/67327-of-shadows-yet-to-come-and-vague-rules-spoilers-ahead?p=67810#post67810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was where you failed, after a couple of hit and misses you should have fudged the results. For example, if you had decreased the soak of the oni by 1 each time they failed to deal damage until they hit the problem would have been solved.<br /> <br /> Other suggestion would be to see that it was a standoff and so the Oni leaves the players with whatever they want due to his master's orders, he was tired, he got what he was looking for... That way the plot could continue to move and the players would see that they cannot defeat all enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a good way to do it with superhero campaigns too, often in them a draw is a win for the players as well. Breaking players out of the D&amp;D mindset is the hardest part of that style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T17:12:07-08:00","id":69510,"title":"","content":"They eventually wound up setting the oni on fire (see, that's where the fire part of my questions comes in :3) and the 'brick' of the group tossed him. Come to realize later, even with his super strength, it'd only be about 12 yards, easy enough for the oni to catch up and continue fighting... but I ruled he went flying and they made their escape. So yes, &quot;Oddjob&quot; is still out there. I'm seriously considering having him become Fatebound considering that fight, and show up repeatedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2221-dtorakhan","name":"DTorakhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}